# The functions that still name an output of a build by a rule of their own,
# or read a file's extension.  Checked by tests/check-program-name.sh.
#
#   file|function|count|pass|reason
#
# "count" is the number of matches in the function; it may only fall.
# "pass" is "owner" for a function the program-name owner (we_progname.c)
# takes over, and "keep" for one that is not the name of an output, with its
# reason.  --strict ignores the "owner" lines.

# --- moved onto the owner with the F9, Run and project path ---
we_prog.c|e_prj_is_program_object|1|owner|"main.o" is named by a literal; which objects enter the library is a build decision the owner keeps as it is
we_prog.c|e_prj_inserted_after_compile|1|owner|"main.o" is named by a literal, as above

# --- moved onto the owner with the debugger ---
we_debug.c|e_d_exe_name_of|2|owner|the program the debugger loads: stem cut and ".e"
we_debug.c|e_d_compile_command|3|owner|the debug binary and its error file: stem cut, ".dbg", ".dbgerr"
we_debug.c|e_d_dap_lang_for|2|owner|which adapter: the end of the name against a table's extension
we_debug.c|e_d_dap_source_ext|2|owner|is this a DAP source: the same end-of-name compare as e_d_dap_lang_for
we_debug.c|e_d_jdb_mark_stop|1|owner|a class named after its source: stem cut
we_debug.c|e_d_brk_jdb_class|1|owner|a class named after its source: stem cut
we_debug.c|e_d_jdb_start_class|1|owner|a class named after its source: stem cut

# --- not the name of an output ---
we_progn.c|e_add_synt_tl|1|keep|a syntax table is chosen by the file's extension; a read, nothing is named
we_ai_ui.c|ai_build_command|1|keep|the compiler for a "Build and fix" read (-fsyntax-only); names no output
we_ai_ws.c|ws_source_like|1|keep|is this file source-like: an extension for a read
we_debug.c|e_d_jdb_class_file|1|keep|a dotted Java class name: the simple name after its last dot
we_debug.c|e_d_jdb_frame_source|1|keep|a dotted Java class name in a stack frame
we_fl_unix.c|e_execute_plan|1|keep|the file the user typed to run; the operand is a source, not an output

# --- rule 5, we_prog.c: the decisions about time and the calls that look at a file ---
we_prog.c|e_build_current|3|keep|the build's one up-to-date rule: the output's time against its source, against the newest object, and the record of what this editor built
we_prog.c|e_build_stat|1|keep|the only stat of a build output, taken in the build's folder
we_prog.c|e_check_header|2|keep|a source and its headers: their times against the output's, as the compile always asked
we_prog.c|e_make_library|1|keep|ar -cr when the library is absent; a library this editor did not build is removed first
we_prog.c|e_cmd_in_path|1|keep|is a command on PATH: names no output
we_prog.c|e_make_multifile_hint|2|keep|looks for the folder's Makefile: names no output
we_prog.c|e_create_project|1|keep|is the project file there: a source, not an output
we_prog.c|e_new_message|1|keep|is the Messages file there: not a build output
we_prog.c|e_p_file_exists|1|keep|is a file there: asked of a source by name
we_prog.c|e_project_is_open|1|keep|is the project file there: a source, not an output
we_prog.c|e_run_sh_make_runnable|1|keep|the mode of the script the user runs: not a build output
